1. Relational Model: Data in tables (rows & columns).
2. Entity-Relationship (ER) Model: Graphical representation of entities and relationships.
3. NoSQL Models: Key-value, document, columnar, and graph databases (MongoDB, Cassandra).

Example ER Diagram Concepts:
Entity: Student, Employee
Attribute: Name, RollNo, Salary
Relationship: “Enrolled in”, “Works in”
